text:
Halves of a drop of dew

with which the sea, on drinking it,

in the depth of its cold breast

congeals a single pearl;

atoms of the rose's perfume

that the wind rocks together;


notes the melodious harp vibrates,

equal in sound;

double stars that in the high sky

describe one orbit;

twin souls that on the sad earth

live from one thought;

these, without doubt, are those who love each other,

keeping their faith entire,

and perhaps, when they die here, they will pass

to love each other in another sphere.

